 402:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h **** /**
 403:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * This is a convenience function which handles the complete MAVLink parsing.
 404:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * the function will parse one byte at a time and return the complete packet once
 405:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * it could be successfully decoded. This function will return 0, 1 or
 406:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * 2 (MAVLINK_FRAMING_INCOMPLETE, MAVLINK_FRAMING_OK or MAVLINK_FRAMING_BAD_CRC)
 407:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *
 408:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * Messages are parsed into an internal buffer (one for each channel). When a complete
 409:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * message is received it is copies into *r_message and the channel's status is
 410:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * copied into *r_mavlink_status.
 411:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *
 412:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param chan     ID of the channel to be parsed.
 413:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *                 A channel is not a physical message channel like a serial port, but a logical pa
 414:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *                 the communication streams. COMM_NB is the limit for the number of channels
 415:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *                 on MCU (e.g. ARM7), while COMM_NB_HIGH is the limit for the number of channels i
 416:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param c        The char to parse
 417:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *
 418:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param r_message NULL if no message could be decoded, the message data else
 419:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @param r_mavlink_status if a message was decoded, this is filled with the channel's stats
 420:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * @return 0 if no message could be decoded, 1 on good message and CRC, 2 on bad CRC
 421:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  *
 422:Service/../MAVLink/common/../mavlink_helpers.h ****  * A typical use scenario of this function call is:
